{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"type-traits-if-constexpr","title":"Type Traits & if constexpr","group":"Templates & Generic Programming","order":46,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>&lt;type_traits&gt;</code> lets templates ask questions about types at compile time; <code>if constexpr</code> (C++17) keeps only the branch that applies, so each instantiation compiles just the code it needs.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-help\"></i>Asking questions about types</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;type_traits&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::boolalpha\n              &lt;&lt; std::is_integral_v&lt;int&gt; &lt;&lt; ' '\n              &lt;&lt; std::is_floating_point_v&lt;int&gt; &lt;&lt; ' '\n              &lt;&lt; std::is_pointer_v&lt;char*&gt; &lt;&lt; ' '\n              &lt;&lt; std::is_same_v&lt;std::remove_const_t&lt;const int&gt;, int&gt; &lt;&lt; ' '\n              &lt;&lt; std::is_trivially_copyable_v&lt;std::string&gt; &lt;&lt; ' '\n              &lt;&lt; std::is_base_of_v&lt;std::exception, std::runtime_error&gt; &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n    static_assert(std::is_same_v&lt;std::decay_t&lt;const int&amp;&gt;, int&gt;);\n    static_assert(sizeof(long long) == 8, \"this code assumes 64-bit long long\");\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true false true true false true</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Trait</th><th>Question / transformation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>is_integral_v&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code>is_floating_point_v&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code>is_arithmetic_v&lt;T&gt;</code></td><td>Category checks</td></tr><tr><td><code>is_same_v&lt;A, B&gt;</code></td><td>Exactly the same type?</td></tr><tr><td><code>is_base_of_v&lt;B, D&gt;</code>, <code>is_convertible_v&lt;From, To&gt;</code></td><td>Relationships</td></tr><tr><td><code>remove_reference_t&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code>remove_const_t&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code>decay_t&lt;T&gt;</code></td><td>Strip qualifiers (decay = what pass-by-value does)</td></tr><tr><td><code>conditional_t&lt;Cond, A, B&gt;</code></td><td>Compile-time ternary on types</td></tr><tr><td><code>enable_if_t&lt;Cond, T&gt;</code></td><td>Remove an overload unless <code>Cond</code> (pre-C++20 SFINAE)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-git-branch\"></i><code>if constexpr</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;type_traits&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\ntemplate &lt;typename T&gt;\nstd::string describe(const T&amp; value) {\n    if constexpr (std::is_integral_v&lt;T&gt;)\n        return \"integer \" + std::to_string(value * 2);     // only compiled for integers\n    else if constexpr (std::is_floating_point_v&lt;T&gt;)\n        return \"float \" + std::to_string(value);\n    else if constexpr (requires { value.size(); })         // C++20 requires-expression\n        return \"sized thing of \" + std::to_string(value.size());\n    else\n        return \"something else\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; describe(21) &lt;&lt; '\\n' &lt;&lt; describe(0.5) &lt;&lt; '\\n'\n              &lt;&lt; describe(std::vector&lt;int&gt;{1, 2, 3}) &lt;&lt; '\\n' &lt;&lt; describe(nullptr) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>integer 42\nfloat 0.500000\nsized thing of 3\nsomething else</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>With a plain <code>if</code>, <em>both</em> branches must compile for every <code>T</code> — <code>value * 2</code> on a <code>std::vector</code> would be an error. <code>if constexpr</code> discards the untaken branch inside templates.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-tool\"></i>Writing your own trait</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;list&gt;\n#include &lt;type_traits&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\ntemplate &lt;typename T&gt; struct is_vector : std::false_type {};\ntemplate &lt;typename T, typename A&gt; struct is_vector&lt;std::vector&lt;T, A&gt;&gt; : std::true_type {};\ntemplate &lt;typename T&gt; inline constexpr bool is_vector_v = is_vector&lt;T&gt;::value;\n\nint main() {\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; is_vector_v&lt;std::vector&lt;int&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt; is_vector_v&lt;std::list&lt;int&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt; is_vector_v&lt;int&gt; &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>100</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is SFINAE?</summary><div><p><em>Substitution Failure Is Not An Error</em>: if substituting template arguments into a function template's signature produces invalid code, that overload is silently dropped instead of causing an error. Pre-C++20 code uses it (via <code>std::enable_if</code>) to constrain templates; C++20 concepts express the same thing readably.</p></div></details></section>"}